  "body": "Closes #807\nClaim: cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet)\n\n### Problem\nThe line between the last read message and the first new one (`div.separator1`, `TopicHTMLBuilder.swift:64-97`) was drawn like any quiet separator (`1px dashed var(--separator)`), unlike legacy, and nothing says where reading resumes.\n\n### Cause\n`reader.css` had no rule for legacy's `--color-separator-new-message`.\n\n### Change (CSS only: the markup, the builder and the CSP are unchanged)\n- Parity @ 87fe0d1c: modern style `2px solid` (`style-liste-light.css:27, 134-136`), classic `1px dashed` (`style-liste.css:24, 124-126`), colour = legacy's `rgba(0,0,0,0.4)`, expressed as 40 % of `--text` so it follows dark and the themes. The legacy dark sheet (`style-liste-dark.css`) has no `.separator1` rule and no such variable (grep), so there is no dark value to port: this is the choice made for it.\n- Deliberate gap (operator, 2026-11-11): a « Nouveau » chip, `::after` generated content centred on the line, accent background. Only the line carries it, so it never shows after the last message of a page (the builder writes no line there) nor without a flag. VoiceOver reads generated content where the line sits. A vertical margin (none in legacy) makes room for the chip.\n- MP threads use the same builder and sheet.\n- Not settled here: screenshots (light/dark, both styles, densities) and the VoiceOver/Dynamic Type check; the issue asks for them and for the operator's device check, so #807 should stay open for that: this PR is `Closes` only if the operator accepts the CSS as is.\n\n### Tests\n`ReaderSeparatorStyleTests` (new): per-style rule, stronger than `--separator`, one chip rule on the line only, the word « Nouveau » never in the generated page. Existing `TopicHTMLBuilderTests.theFlagMessageIsFollowedByTheLegacySeparatorUnlessLast` keeps covering « never after the last message / no flag ». Not run (Linux session).\n\n### Ledger\n\n```gap-new\nSection: Reader\n| GAP-807 | New-message line | Line between read and new messages: 2px solid (modern) or 1px dashed (classic), no label. | `style-liste-light.css:134-136`, `style-liste.css:124-126` @ `87fe0d1c` | Same line per style, with a « Nouveau » chip centred on it (CSS only); colour follows the text colour in dark. | LOT-034, #807 | UX change | operator device test 2026-11-11 (#807) | b·operator |\n```\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CDvQG8jqNrseTphdnF)_",
